  "content": {
    "title": "'KPop Demon Hunters' meals coming to McDonald's. Here's when.",
    "text": "March 24, 2026Updated March 31, 2026, 4:20 p.m. ETThe KPop battle between Huntr/X and Saja Boys is coming to McDonald's.The fast-food giant will begin offering a pair of meals inspired by the Netflix film \"KPop Demon Hunters,\" beginning March 31.Each meal includes a collectible card pack featuring a photocard of art featuring either Huntr/X or the Saja Boys, and a Derpy the Tiger access card with a QR code that unlocks exclusive content via the McDonald's app. That content is \"a special reveal of the group that wins the Battle for the Fans,\" according to a McDonald's news release.The animated movie \"KPop Demon Hunters\" is about a South Korean pop girl group, Huntr/X, that battles demons with music. The Saja Boys, a boy band made up of demons, attempt to disrupt that mission. The soundtrack has been a hit, and the film won two Oscars – one for the song \"Golden\" and another for best animated feature film. A sequel is in the works.\"With McDonald's, we were able to turn the rivalry between The Saja Boys and Huntr/X into something fans can actually experience, drawing inspiration from Korean culture and food traditions that sit at the heart of the film,\" said Marian Lee, chief marketing officer for Netflix, in the news release.What's in the 'KPop Demon Hunters\" meals at McDonald's?McDonald's will begin serving a Huntr/X Meal, featuring McNuggets, and a Saja Boys breakfast meal, which comes with a Spicy Saja McMuffin, starting Tuesday, March 31. Here's what's in each meal:The Huntr/X Meal: A 10-piece order of Chicken McNuggets, medium soft drink and Ramyeon McShaker Fries, which have a soy, garlic, sesame and spice seasoning inspired by Rumi, Mira and Zoey's go-to noodle snack. You sprinkle the seasoning into the McShaker bag, toss in the fries and shake to distribute the seasoning on the fries. The meal also comes with Hunter Sauce, described as \"a sweet chili sauce mixing notes of chili, garlic and pepper with just enough heat,\" and Demon Sauce, which is \"a bold mustard sauce with heat and tang – made purple, just like demon patterns.\"The Saja Boys Breakfast Meal: The Sausage McMuffin with Egg, comes topped with a peppery Spicy Saja Sauce. You also get Hash Browns and a small soft drink.\"From Ramyeon McShaker Fries to Demon sauces paired with Soda Pop, every detail was designed to feel like it could have come straight out of a scene in the movie,\" said Netflix's Lee.What is the new 'KPop Demon Hunters\" McFlurry at McDonald's?McDonald's also has a new-flavored dessert inspired by Derpy the Tiger, also from the animated film. The Derpy McFlurry, blends creamy vanilla soft serve with berry popping pearls in a wild berry sauce.\"Big things happen when you bring two massive fandoms together, and this partnership was a natural fit,\" Alyssa Buetikofer, chief marketing and customer experience officer at McDonald's, said in the news release. \"We found authentic ways to unite our iconic worlds – inviting Huntr/X and Saja Boys fans into the rivalry in ways that feel true to the film and unmistakably McDonald's.\"Mike Snider is a national trending news reporter for USA TODAY. You can follow him on Threads, Bluesky, X and email him at mikegsnider & @mikegsnider.bsky.social & @mikesnider & msnider@usatoday.com.",
